==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} ''[[mund]]'', from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*munþaz}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*ment-}}. Cognate with Low German {{term|Mund|lang=nds}}, Dutch {{term|mond|lang=nl}}, English {{term|mouth|lang=en}}, Danish {{term|mund|lang=da}}.

